tion, in all regions. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19561, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01HsqZsHfLEF2sPANbaZNRnf", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19561, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HsqZsHfLEF2sPANbaZNRnf", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 23474, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened incident INC-0001 (SEV2), which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging before it went to production.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions now run it, and the error rate has dropped to 0.2%. Because v2.3.0 had been healthy in production before, the rollback didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Incident:** The summary says what failed and what I did. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure should be found before anyone redeploys it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HnNXq9Zcy39H8fERYNMA2r", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018EkLJ8B2Y7FhVmCEp5mWpZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LbXWozDzkgejTJspDU2wSv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HJohq7u38Cs5x9GZsZuXfA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NnarzCGNHpZ5NaPs3N4djq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HsqZsHfLEF2sPANbaZNRnf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production, the service failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. (v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging.) The SRE agent rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all regions. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened incident INC-0001 (SEV2), which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging before it went to production.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions now run it, and the error rate has dropped to 0.2%. Because v2.3.0 had been healthy in production before, the rollback didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Incident:** The summary says what failed and what I did. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure should be found before anyone redeploys it.", "type": "text"}]}]}